1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,546
Orchard Core is an open-source content management system and application framework for ASP.NET Core.

2
00:00:07,546 --> 00:00:11,745
In this video, you'll see what it is, how a site is organized,

3
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:14,030
and what you can build with it.

4
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:22,374
Orchard Core is open source, modular, and multi-tenant.

5
00:00:22,374 --> 00:00:23,786
It has two parts:

6
00:00:23,786 --> 00:00:28,513
the Orchard Core Framework, and the Orchard Core CMS, which is built on

7
00:00:28,513 --> 00:00:30,170
top of the framework.

8
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:37,027
The framework is for developers who build modular, multi-tenant applications on ASP.NET Core,

9
00:00:37,027 --> 00:00:39,802
such as software as a service products.

10
00:00:39,802 --> 00:00:43,380
It is distributed on its own, separate from the CMS.

11
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:48,761
The CMS is for building websites that you manage from an admin interface.

12
00:00:48,761 --> 00:00:52,630
It includes content management, themes, and user management.

13
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:54,740
This video focuses on the CMS.

14
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:02,135
This is a website built with the Orchard Core CMS:

15
00:01:02,135 --> 00:01:06,129
a blog, with a menu that has Home and About, and a post to read.

16
00:01:06,129 --> 00:01:08,640
It is the front end, drawn by a theme.

17
00:01:09,106 --> 00:01:12,124
The people who run the site work in the admin.

18
00:01:12,124 --> 00:01:17,406
Its welcome page has cards such as Create content, Customize theme, and Manage users.

19
00:01:17,873 --> 00:01:20,973
The menu on the left leads to everything else.

20
00:01:20,973 --> 00:01:25,803
Content is for what you publish, Design is for themes, widgets, and content

21
00:01:25,803 --> 00:01:28,843
types, and Tools is for features and recipes.

22
00:01:33,131 --> 00:01:37,047
Content, Content Items opens the Manage Content page.

23
00:01:37,047 --> 00:01:41,892
Each row is one content item, with its title, its type, its status,

24
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:46,141
such as Published or Draft, and when it was last modified.

25
00:01:46,742 --> 00:01:48,687
Let's open About with Edit.

26
00:01:48,687 --> 00:01:52,871
The editor shows the pieces that the item's type is made of, such

27
00:01:52,871 --> 00:01:57,232
as Title, Permalink, and HtmlBody, which holds the body of the item.

28
00:01:57,694 --> 00:02:00,493
Publish makes your changes visible on the site.

29
00:02:00,493 --> 00:02:04,771
Save Draft stores them without publishing, and Preview shows the page as it

30
00:02:04,771 --> 00:02:07,464
will look on the site, before you publish it.

31
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:12,485
Behind every content item is a content type.

32
00:02:12,485 --> 00:02:18,640
Design, Content Definition, Content Types lists them, such as Article, Blog, and Page.

33
00:02:20,615 --> 00:02:22,082
Let's open Article.

34
00:02:22,082 --> 00:02:25,015
A content type is a set of fields and parts.

35
00:02:25,015 --> 00:02:29,826
Fields hold values such as Subtitle and Banner Image, and parts add behavior

36
00:02:29,826 --> 00:02:35,635
that many types share, such as Title, Autoroute for the permalink, and HtmlBody for the body.

37
00:02:36,164 --> 00:02:39,614
Add Field and Add Parts extend a type from this screen, so you

38
00:02:39,614 --> 00:02:42,404
can shape your content without leaving the admin.

39
00:02:46,704 --> 00:02:49,383
Design, Themes lists the installed themes.

40
00:02:49,383 --> 00:02:54,629
The current Site theme draws the front end, and the current Admin theme draws the admin.

41
00:02:54,629 --> 00:02:57,364
Make Current changes which theme is in use.

42
00:02:57,829 --> 00:03:01,878
A zone is a named section of a theme's layout, and a widget

43
00:03:01,878 --> 00:03:04,620
is a block of content shown in a zone.

44
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:08,545
Design, Widgets lists the zones, here Content and Footer.

45
00:03:08,545 --> 00:03:12,159
The Footer zone holds one widget, also named Footer.

46
00:03:12,622 --> 00:03:15,797
A layer decides on which pages its widgets appear.

47
00:03:15,797 --> 00:03:20,162
The Always layer shows them on every page, and the Homepage layer shows

48
00:03:20,162 --> 00:03:22,032
them only on the home page.

49
00:03:26,295 --> 00:03:30,887
Orchard Core is built from modules, and each module provides features.

50
00:03:30,887 --> 00:03:35,721
Tools, Features lists them by category, with a description of each one and

51
00:03:35,721 --> 00:03:37,715
the features it depends on.

52
00:03:38,194 --> 00:03:40,657
Search narrows the list as you type.

53
00:03:40,657 --> 00:03:44,468
Let's search for Workflows, which is disabled on this site.

54
00:03:44,468 --> 00:03:48,455
Enable turns a feature on, and Disable turns it off, so a site

55
00:03:48,455 --> 00:03:50,214
uses only what it needs.

56
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:54,365
A recipe sets up a site in one go.

57
00:03:54,365 --> 00:04:02,019
Depending on the recipe, it enables features, defines content types, chooses themes, and creates starting content.

58
00:04:02,019 --> 00:04:06,674
The Setup screen runs one, and this blog came from the Blog recipe.

59
00:04:07,424 --> 00:04:12,585
Deployment plans build packages that move content and configuration between sites.

60
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:17,042
Importing a package runs it as a recipe, and Remote Deployment sends a

61
00:04:17,042 --> 00:04:19,564
package to another Orchard Core site.

62
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:26,082
Orchard Core is multi-tenant.

63
00:04:26,082 --> 00:04:32,374
One running application hosts many independent sites, called tenants, and each tenant has

64
00:04:32,374 --> 00:04:35,354
its own URL, content, users, and theme.

65
00:04:36,104 --> 00:04:42,442
You manage tenants from the Default tenant, in Multi-Tenancy, Tenants, once the Tenants feature is enabled.

66
00:04:42,442 --> 00:04:45,414
Each tenant is set up with a recipe of its own.

67
00:04:49,614 --> 00:04:54,123
A full CMS site uses a theme and templates to render your content,

68
00:04:54,123 --> 00:04:56,816
with little or no custom development.

69
00:04:56,816 --> 00:05:00,824
The Blog, Agency, and Coming Soon recipes each set one up.

70
00:05:01,574 --> 00:05:07,838
A decoupled site keeps the admin, and your own ASP.NET Core pages render the content.

71
00:05:07,838 --> 00:05:15,134
A headless site only manages content, and another application reads it through GraphQL or REST APIs.

72
00:05:15,884 --> 00:05:21,249
With the framework alone, you build your own modular, multi-tenant application, such as

73
00:05:21,249 --> 00:05:25,344
a software as a service product, without any of the CMS features.

74
00:05:29,544 --> 00:05:34,559
The Orchard Core documentation has reference pages for the built-in modules.

75
00:05:34,559 --> 00:05:40,124
The Modules Reference groups them by area, such as Content, Design, and Localization.

76
00:05:40,874 --> 00:05:45,925
The Glossary explains the terms you met here, such as content item, content

77
00:05:45,925 --> 00:05:48,294
type, tenant, layer, and recipe.

78
00:05:49,044 --> 00:05:52,838
Other videos in this series cover setting up your first site and finding

79
00:05:52,838 --> 00:05:54,394
your way around the admin.

80
00:05:56,394 --> 00:06:03,192
Orchard Core is a modular, multi-tenant framework, and a CMS built on it, for ASP.NET Core.

81
00:06:03,192 --> 00:06:05,014
Thanks for watching.

